# Local tooling state (never published)
.fleet/

# Python bytecode from scripts/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Agent-harness scratch. These are per-run notes from the grok-fleet pipeline;
# tracking them shipped a stale task brief and a failed test log inside the
# source tarball and every goreleaser archive.
.review.md
.task.md

# Scratch a parallel agent leaves in the tree. Every pattern here is something
# that actually turned up in `git status` during the 1.0.3 sweep, not a
# precaution: a coverage-attribution step wrote empty flattened copies
# (internal_oauth2_github_test.go) into the repository root, and a probe run
# left zz_tmp_probe*_test.go files that were captured by a commit and had to be
# amended out.
#
# The repository root holds no Go package, so a *_test.go file there is always
# scratch; the leading slash keeps this from touching the real suites.
/*_test.go
zz_tmp_*
/*.cover.out
/before.out
/after.out

# Compiled commands. `go build ./cmd/<name>` without -o drops the binary in the
# repository root, where a `git add -A` would otherwise commit 13 MB of object
# code into an unrelated change. tests/spec/tracked_artifacts_test.go enforces
# that every cmd/ name appears here.
/admin-gateway
/bridge
/recover
/vault

# Grok review deliverables. The fleet writes its findings here inside the
# sandbox worktree, and the harness commits whatever it finds. They are review
# output rather than product, and they are archived to /mnt/knowledge instead.
GROK_OUTPUT.md
